solution:
The numerator \(10^7\) contains seven factors of \(10\), while \(10^4\) in the denominator contains four. Canceling those four nonzero factors leaves three factors of \(10\) in the numerator:
\[
\frac{10^7}{5\times10^4}
=\frac{10\times10\times10}{5}
=\frac{1000}{5}
=200.
\]
The value is \(200\), choice \(\mathrm{D}\).

